{"text": "Revenues made a strong comeback in the services sector last month, according to respondents to the latest survey from the Federal Reserve Bank in Richmond. After several months of relatively weak performances, both retail and other services businesses saw a rise in revenues and shopper traffic. Services employment gained strength in both retail and non-retail establishments, and wage pressures gathered steam. Increases in non-retail wages, however, grew at the same tepid rate as last month. Looking ahead, retail businesses expressed much greater optimism about demand, and non-retail businesses also had a brighter outlook than they did in March. On the price front, services prices increased more sharply in the retail sector, but made only modest advances in non-retail establishments. In addition, the outlook for overall price increases in the next six months, though still at modest levels, was the highest so far this year.\n\n<ts></ts>", "timeseries": [{"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 33.0, 32.0, 50.0, 37.0, 22.0, 15.0, 26.0, 24.0, 17.0, 8.0, 7.0, 13.0, 20.0, 57.0, 23.0, 33.0, 29.0, 16.0, 24.0, 22.0, 10.0, 3.0, 19.0, 4.0, 13.0, 20.0, 42.0, 19.0, 40.0, 17.0, 27.0], "unit": "nonretail_demand_fut", "freq": "1M"}, {"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 3.0, -3.0, -11.0, -1.0, -14.0, 6.0, -9.0, 19.0, 2.0, 3.0, 1.0, -6.0, -5.0, 2.0, 13.0, 9.0, 14.0, 9.0, 6.0, -1.0, -3.0, 6.0, -7.0, -12.0, -6.0, -6.0, -6.0, -20.0, 11.0, 11.0, 13.0], "unit": "nonretail_employment", "freq": "1M"}, {"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 32.0, 21.0, 18.0, 15.0, 12.0, 10.0, 20.0, 30.0, 20.0, 8.0, 21.0, 20.0, 6.0, 21.0, 17.0, 14.0, 8.0, 21.0, 18.0, 17.0, 20.0, 29.0, 27.0, 9.0, 12.0, 5.0, 2.0, 16.0, 24.0, 6.0, 6.0], "unit": "nonretail_wages", "freq": "1M"}, {"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 1.23, 1.36, 0.87, 0.87, 1.35, 1.01, 1.32, 1.62, 1.72, 1.92, 1.55, 1.13, 0.92, 1.24, 1.53, 1.76, 1.87, 1.46, 1.69, 1.07, 1.68, 1.14, 1.24, 1.59, 1.26, 2.75, 1.1, 1.18, 1.11, 0.65