{"text": "Services Sector Sector For the first time since August of 2000, the overall services sector revenues index moved into positive territory, at an index of 11 compared to -12 a month ago. The seasonally adjusted services sector employment index was still negative, but less so at -8, from -13 in March. Supported by retail wage growth, the overall average wage index moved up to 22 from March's 15. The optimism index for services businesses climbed to 36 in April, well above the 20 registered in March.\n\n<ts></ts>", "timeseries": [{"values": [null, null, null, null, null, -5.0, -9.0, -5.0, -1.0, -11.0, 11.0, -7.0, 16.0, 13.0, 4.0, -1.0, -1.0, 3.0, -1.0, 5.0, 9.0, 6.0, 5.0, 0.0, -7.0, -8.0, 9.0, -16.0, -9.0, -2.0, -4.0, -8.0, -25.0, -15.0, -13.0, -8.0], "unit": "employment", "freq": "1M"}, {"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 9.0, 0.0, 19.0, 4.0, 8.0, 19.0, 22.0, 23.0, 33.0, 25.0, 6.0, 6.0, 8.0, 20.0, 13.0, 26.0, 16.0, 17.0, 9.0, 18.0, 7.0, -3.0, 17.0, -1.0, -7.0, -4.0, -14.0, -22.0, -21.0, -12.0, 11.0], "unit": "revenues", "freq": "1M"}, {"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 28.0, 22.0, 24.0, 24.0, 21.0, 25.0, 36.0, 39.0, 29.0, 20.0, 18.0, 22.0, 20.0, 25.0, 24.0, 17.0, 25.0, 35.0, 21.0, 27.0, 24.0, 27.0, 32.0, 29.0, 20.0, 19.0, 14.0, 17.0, 15.0, 15.0, 22.0], "unit": "wages", "freq": "1M"}], "task_type": "world_knowledge", "text_quality": "real", "series_id": "rich_svc_2001-04_b2", "dataset": "richmond_nonmanufacturing", "source": "https://www.richmondfed.org/research/regional_economy/surveys_of_business_conditions/service_sector", "license": "public-domain-us-gov", "text_source": "first_party_official", "alignment": "recites", "domain": "macro_econ", "region": "US", "period_start": "1998-05-01", "period_end": "2001-04-01", "meta": {"bank": "Federal Reserve Bank of Richmond", "survey": "Fifth District Survey of Service Sector Activity", "district": 5, "sector": "non-manufacturing", "release_date": "2001-05-08", "data_month": "2001-04", "section_heading": "Overall", "block_ordinal": 2, "headline": "Fifth District Services-Sector Activity", "n_points": 36, "channels": ["employment", "revenues", "wages"], "series_vintage": "as-published (stitched from each release's own table, real-time as of this release)", "narrative_format": "narr_html", "table_format": "tbl_html", "figures_in_text": 7, "recited_channel": "employment"}}
{"text": "The big story in retail was that sales revenues shot up to an index of 20, compared to -6 in March. Big ticket sales registered an index value of 2, smartly above the -35 in March. Shopper traffic was also improved, with the index rebounding from -9 the previous month to 21 in April. Inventories remained a problem, though, with the index reaching 29 compared to -4 last month. Retailers' optimism increased; the index registered 58 compared to 30 in March. The seasonally adjusted employment index for retail establishments jumped to 7 from -23 a month ago. The pressure in average wages showed no letup, as the retail wage growth index surged to 58 from 37 in March.\n\n<ts></ts>", "timeseries": [{"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 13.0, -5.0, 12.0, -3.0, 1.0, 27.0, 19.0, 10.0, 16.0, 23.0, -11.0, -18.0, 11.0, -2.0, -12.0, 4.0, 39.0, 15.0, -18.0, -1.0, -37.0, -36.0, -22.0, -9.0, -40.0, -21.0, -37.0, -68.0, -44.0, -35.0, 2.0], "unit": "retail_big_ticket_sales", "freq": "1M"}, {"values": [null, null, null, null, null, -15.0, -18.0, 2.0, -3.0, -11.0, 4.0, -4.0, 9.0, 26.0, 9.0, 0.0, 3.0, 12.0, -5.0, -4.0, 9.0, -5.0, 5.0, -9.0, -14.0, -11.0, -1.0, -17.0, -7.0, 1.0, -3.0, -8.0, -41.0, -41.0, -23.0, 7.0], "unit": "retail_employment", "freq": "1M"}, {"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 16.0, 13.0, -11.0, 7.0, 13.0, 12.0, -3.0, 12.0, 22.0, 2.0, 9.0, 6.0, 27.0, 16.0, -6.0, 15.0, 22.0, 47.0, 13.0, 40.0, 12.0, 21.0, 6.0, 0.0, 35.0, 35.0, 50.0, 0.0, 0.0, -4.0, 29.0], "unit": "retail_inventories", "freq": "1M"}, {"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 21.0, 1.0, 37.0, 13.0, 45.0, 44.0, 33.0, 11.0, 52.0, 30.0, 3.0, 20.0, 40.0, 21.0, 18.0, 40.0, 19.0, 33.0, 2.0, 40.0, -1.0, 9.0, 18.0, 21.0, -30.0, -29.0, -17.0, -55.0, -33.0, -6.0, 20.0], "unit": "retail_revenues", "freq": "1M"}, {"values": [null, null, null, null, null, 32.0, -9.0, 27.0, -3.0, 29.0, 29.0, 20.0, -2.0, 22.0, 14.0, -14.0, 0.0, 18.0, 12.0, 18.0, -32.0, 34.0, 23.0, -13.0, 27.0, -6.0, -1.0, 12.0, -7.0, -2